 "asked_at": "2026-10-18T00:45+08:00",
 "answer": "Yes, the haze in KL is bad today. Readings are in the \"unhealthy\" range.\n\n**KL today (Sat, 17 Oct, as of 9:30am):** In Kuala Lumpur, Cheras recorded 162 and Batu Muda 159, while Putrajaya also registered 162. For context, API readings of zero to 50 indicate good air quality, 51 to 100 moderate, 101 to 200 unhealthy, 201 to 300 very unhealthy, and above 300 hazardous.\n\n**Nearby Klang Valley areas are similar:** Klang recorded 171, Johan Setia 170, Petaling Jaya and Shah Alam 169 each, and Banting 153. Across Malaysia, 24 areas recorded unhealthy air quality as of 9.30am, with Pasir Gudang, Johor, registering the highest API reading at 196.\n\n**Trend:** The haze has been going on for about a week. Yesterday some stations went past the \"very unhealthy\" mark, with 29 areas recording unhealthy or worse air, and Larkin and Pasir Gudang hitting an API of 202.\n\n**Tips:**\n- Cut down on time outdoors, especially exercise. Under the official guidelines, outdoor activities would be postponed when the API reading exceeds 100, while schools would be closed when the reading exceeds 200.\n- If you have to go out, wear an N95 mask. Keep your windows closed and run an air purifier if you have one.\n- Children, older people, and anyone with asthma or heart or lung conditions should be especially careful.\n\nThe readings change throughout the day. For live numbers, check the Department of Environment's APIMS website or the MyIPU app.",
